                <note rend="inline" type="source">862S.01/17: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Belgium</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brussels</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1923-02-03T22:00:00+00:00"><hi rendition="#italic">February 3,
                                1923—10 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received February 4—5:10
                        p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>23. Department’s telegram 15, February 2, 7 p.m. Have communicated informally to
                    the Minister of Foreign Affairs the substance of Department’s telegram received
                    late today. He agreed with Department’s suggestions and expressed willingness to
                    sign treaty at our convenience. He also said that, “It was not the intention of
                    the Belgian Government to deny to American missionaries in the mandated
                    territory of Ruanda-Urundi the enjoyment of privileges heretofore accorded them
                    in that territory.”…</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
